:: Cursed Shop Intro
<<generate1>><<person1>>
You climb up the ladder the request pointed you to and arrive at a window lit with ominous purple light. As you open the door, a thick mist pools down the railings into the alleyway.
<br><br>
The window is shut behind you once you climb inside. The room you find yourself in is lit with a purple glow, eminating from the mist that has no discernable source. The walls are adorned with various masks, chains, talismans, and other strange paraphernalia.
<br><br>
Perhaps most eyecatching, at the end of the room, there stands a <<person>> you cant quite make out. <<His>> form blurs at the edges and <<his>> face is covered with what looks like a mask. The mask resembles a mirror, broken, yet reflecting your own shattered face in the shards.
<br><br>
A voice eminates from the <<personsimple>>, though it does not seem to be muffled by the mask obscuring <<his>> face, "I'm glad you came, though I knew the inevitability of it all. You would have ended up here sooner or later. Let me have a look at you."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Cursed Shop Intro 2]]>><</link>>

:: Cursed Shop Intro 2
<<endevent>>
<<generate1>><<person1>>
The <<person>> stumbles as <<he>> draws close. The movements are more like a marionette dancing on strings than a living thing. As <<he>> draws close, you are hit with the smell of incense and a thick underlying smell you can't identify.
<br><br>
Looking into the reflection, you can see yourself, but the warped surface of the mirror shows a you that you aren't used to. The figure speaks once more, "Let me explain why I have called you here. It is my site you have been using you see."
<br><br>
<<if $transformationParts.traits.strongnose is "default">>
As the shopkeeper draws near, you can finally place the smell. It's rot. A thick oppressive smell of rot, covered by incense and clothing. You try to hide your discomfort as <<he>> continue.
<br><br>
<</if>>
"You have peaked my interest in your work so far. I set up this little shop for you to buy goods to make your work easier. Keep doing well and perhaps we can work out some more special deals. Until then, work hard."
