:: Missing Children Intro
The <<personsimple>> who answers the door looks to you with a concerned and tired look. "The missing children? Listen, I really don't have time for this. I have my own children and I can't deal with you distracting me."
<br><br>
You look past the <<person>>'s frame into <<his>> small house. You hear something... strange inside, like the sound of dragging chains. The <<personsimple>>, seeming to hear the sound as well, turns around in a hurry and rushes back into <<his>> home. 
<br><br>
The house is quiet, nothing but the sound of a panicking <<father>> and the breeze through an open window.
<br><br>
<<link [[Examine outside the window (0:10)|Missing Children]]>><<endevent>><<pass 10>><</link>>

:: Missing Children
You walk around the small Domus home and look around the window. Some claw markings remain on the frame and large heavy hoof prints are embedded into the hard winter soil.
<br><br>
<<if $skulduggery gte 800 or $transformationParts.traits.sharpEyes is "default" or $transformationParts.dragon.eyes isnot "disabled">>
As you look closer, a barely visible light trail is evident where chains have been dragged through the dirt. Black fur clings to a nearby branch. Whatever this is, it's definitely not human.
<br><br>
<</if>>
You follow the tracks from house to house. You can usually hear the muffled wails through the walls. It's heartbreaking to hear, you try to tone it out.
<br><br>
Eventually the tracks end at the forest. It seems whatever has been kidnapping the children has retreated to possibly its home. Trailing it may be a bad idea without sufficient preparation.
<br><br>
<<link [[Follow the trail into the forest (2:00)|Missing Children 2]]>><<pass 120>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Give up the request|Missing Children Fail]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Missing Children 2
<<beastNEWinit 1 creature>>
<<if $NPCList[0].monster is "monster">>
	<<set $NPCList[0].fullDescription to "Krampus">>
	<<set $NPCList[0].type to "Krampus">>
<</if>>
<<saveNPC 0 krampus>>
<<set $payoutmultiplier to 10>>
Disregarding your own safety, you follow the trail into the forest. The trail leads deep, deeper than you've ever gone before. Finally, the trail ends at the entrance of a large den leading under the earth.
<br><br>
You grip the edge of the den and crouch as you slowly make your way into the den carved into damp and cool dirt. A light emits from the deepest depths of the den, reaching your eyes from affar and illuminating the end of the tunnel.
<br><br>
As you reach the end of the tunnel, the room widens into a cave. At the center stands a tall hunched figure. Its body is covered in black fur, large twisting horns adorn its head, cloven hooved feet at the bottom, its pointed sharp claws, the face twisted in a grimace with jagged snaggled teeth exposed. On its back is a basket that twitches and shakes like something is inside.
<br><br>
As it lays its glowing yellow eyes upon you, it lays the huge basket to the floor and turns to you, the chains dragging from the creature's wrists. It lets out a cold thick chortle as it descends upon you.
<br><br>
